  "description": "Beasley's uncapacitated p-median test problems pmed1 to pmed40 from OR-Library: each a weighted undirected graph and the number p of medians to open. Each instance has one edge per vertex pair with its cost (where a file lists a pair more than once, the last cost, as the OR-Library page defines it) and p in its meta; the allocation costs are the graph's shortest-path distances, which the consumer computes. The optimal solution values are in the source pmedopt.txt, which the recipe does not read into the instances.",
